INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '9b1d0e8c-7321-5de0-bd09-6da8d9a86709','Futz','Futz (or futzing) is the deliberate processing of a sound, most often dialogue, to make it seem as if it originates from a device within the scene such as a telephone, radio, television, intercom, or public-address speaker. It typically combines band-limiting EQ, distortion, and sometimes added noise to imitate the limited fidelity of that source.','A futz means processing a sound so it seems to come from a phone, radio, or TV in the scene. You cut the highs and lows and add grit so the voice sounds thin and tinny.','Futzing sells the illusion that a voice or sound comes from an on-screen device, helping the audience believe the story world, and it keeps such source audio separate from the clean, full-range dialogue.','A re-recording mixer builds a futz by band-limiting a dialogue track, for example to a telephone range around 300 Hz to 3 kHz, and adding distortion or noise, usually on a separate futz channel that can be blended with the clean line.','Dialogue Processing',ARRAY['Fricatives','Equalization','Distortion','Worldizing','Dialogue editing']::text[],ARRAY['Futzing so heavily that the dialogue becomes unintelligible; the effect must still let the audience understand the words.','Printing the futz permanently onto the only dialogue track, leaving no clean version if the effect later needs to change.','UNSAFE: Cranking monitor level to judge a thin, distorted futz, pushing dubbing-stage exposure past the OSHA 90 dBA eight-hour limit and risking hearing damage over a long session.']::text[],ARRAY['Creating a phone-call effect for one side of a conversation.','Making a public-address announcement sound like it comes through venue speakers.','Treating a radio or television playing in the background of a scene.']::text[],'739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='9b1d0e8c-7321-5de0-bd09-6da8d9a86709' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Futz'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '9b1d0e8c-7321-5de0-bd09-6da8d9a86709','739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='9b1d0e8c-7321-5de0-bd09-6da8d9a86709' AND gt.achievement_id='739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '01547ac0-2af3-5e57-bf38-f1d9a8c79d16','Futz stem','A futz stem is a submix (stem) that carries dialogue or other sound processed to sound as though it is reproduced by a device or medium within the scene - a telephone, television, radio, intercom, or public-address system - typically through band-limiting, distortion, and added noise. Kept separate from the clean dialogue stem, it lets the futzed treatment be balanced, muted, or swapped independently in the final mix and in alternate deliverables.','To ''futz'' a voice is to change its tone. It then sounds like it comes from a phone, radio, or TV in the scene. A futz stem is a grouped submix that holds only these treated sounds. Mixers keep it apart from the clean voice so they can raise, lower, or swap it on its own.','It isolates in-scene ''device'' sound so the re-recording mixer can control its level and character on its own, and can substitute the clean version when a scene, edit, or alternate-language deliverable requires it.','A re-recording mixer routes phone-side or TV-source dialogue through a futz chain to its own stem, then balances it against the clean dialogue and swaps between them as the picture cuts on and off the device.','Mix Stems',ARRAY['Futz track','Dialogue stem','Print master','Re-recording mix','M&E (Music and Effects)','Fold-down']::text[],ARRAY['Baking the futz effect into the clean dialogue so it can no longer be removed for foreign-language or alternate versions.','Confusing a futz stem, which is a grouped submix, with a single futz track element.','Over-processing the futz so on-device dialogue becomes unintelligible when the story needs it understood.']::text[],ARRAY['Mixing a phone call where the audience hears both the on-scene speaker and the futzed voice from the earpiece.','Delivering separate clean and futz stems so an M&E version can re-voice the device dialogue.','Cutting between a radio broadcast heard in-scene and the same voice heard clean.']::text[],'739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='01547ac0-2af3-5e57-bf38-f1d9a8c79d16' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Futz stem'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '01547ac0-2af3-5e57-bf38-f1d9a8c79d16','739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='01547ac0-2af3-5e57-bf38-f1d9a8c79d16' AND gt.achievement_id='739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '71d9598e-f692-558c-a245-a9fbf79df4d7','Futz track','A futz track is an individual dialogue or effects track element carrying audio deliberately processed to sound as if reproduced by an in-scene device or medium - telephone, radio, television, intercom, or public-address - usually via band-limiting, distortion, and noise. It sits alongside the clean (unfutzed) version so the editor or mixer can choose or blend between them.','''Futz'' means treating a sound so it seems to come from a device in the scene, like a phone speaker. A futz track is one edited track holding that treated sound. It usually sits next to the clean version of the same line. The team can pick or blend the two.','It keeps the processed ''device'' performance as a distinct editable element, so the clean and futzed versions can be compared, blended, or rerouted without redoing the effect.','A dialogue editor lays a filtered, distorted copy of a line on a futz track under the clean line, letting the mixer crossfade to it the moment the shot favors the device.','Dialogue Editing',ARRAY['Futz stem','Dialogue editing','ADR','Worldizing','Perspective','Re-recording mix']::text[],ARRAY['Treating the futz track as the only version and deleting the clean line, leaving no way to pull the effect back.','Confusing a single futz track with a futz stem, which is a grouped submix of such material.','Applying a generic phone filter without matching the specific device''s frequency range and distortion.']::text[],ARRAY['Editing a walkie-talkie exchange with clean and futzed copies of each line.','Preparing a filtered voicemail line to sit under the on-camera actor.','Handing the mixer both versions of a public-address announcement to blend to taste.']::text[],'739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='71d9598e-f692-558c-a245-a9fbf79df4d7' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Futz track'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '71d9598e-f692-558c-a245-a9fbf79df4d7','739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='71d9598e-f692-558c-a245-a9fbf79df4d7' AND gt.achievement_id='739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'db338820-e3b8-54db-a5bd-549fc8d01c8f','Glottal pulse','In the source-filter theory of voice production, the glottal pulse is the quasi-periodic puff of airflow released through the glottis on each opening-and-closing cycle of the vocal folds during voiced phonation. This train of pulses is the voice source (excitation) that the vocal tract then filters into speech; its repetition rate sets the fundamental frequency and its spectrum falls off at roughly 12 dB per octave.','When you speak a vowel, your vocal folds open and close very fast. Each opening lets out a small puff of air. That puff is the glottal pulse. The stream of puffs is the raw buzz of the voice. Your mouth and throat then shape it into words. How fast the puffs repeat sets the pitch.','It is the physical sound source of voiced speech, providing the harmonic-rich excitation whose rate and shape set vocal pitch and much of a voice''s basic timbre before the vocal tract shapes it.','Understanding the glottal pulse helps a dialogue mixer or editor diagnose pitch, roughness, and breathiness, and guides pitch-correction, de-essing, and voice-processing choices.','Voice Acoustics',ARRAY['Formant','Fundamental frequency','Source-filter model','Vocal fry','Nasal-formant control','Harmonics']::text[],ARRAY['Confusing the glottal pulse rate (fundamental frequency) with formants, which are vocal-tract resonances, not the source.','Assuming the glottal source is a pure tone, when it is a harmonic-rich pulse train.','Treating breathy or rough voice quality as a vocal-tract issue when it originates at the glottal source.']::text[],ARRAY['Explaining why pitch shifting changes the pulse rate but not the vowel identity.','Diagnosing vocal fry heard as irregular, widely spaced glottal pulses.','Choosing pitch-correction settings that track the voice''s fundamental.']::text[],'739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='db338820-e3b8-54db-a5bd-549fc8d01c8f' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Glottal pulse'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'db338820-e3b8-54db-a5bd-549fc8d01c8f','739bdba4-0fac-4455-9ee2-1a56096cab92',true
